1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:23,263
The kings held their auction in an old train station because
apparently every building in Midnight City had retired from one job
and started committing a different crime. Nigga, I respected ambition.
The platforms were covered in red carpet. Cars stood where trains used
to stop. A jazz band played on a locomotive with gold wheels.

2
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:46,616
Above everything hung the Crown of Midnight inside a glass case,
turning slowly under a light bright enough to make half the men
beneath it reconsider their marriages. I looked once. Shawna noticed.
"You want it?" "On you first." "It's a king's crown." "Nigga, it's
jewelry until somebody starts arguing." She smiled and hooked her arm
through mine.

3
00:00:46,866 --> 00:01:10,329
We were here because Zero required every finalist to pledge something
at the auction. Not buy. Pledge. A house, a fleet, a loyalty.
Something the council could seize if a claimant withdrew. I had no
intention of withdrawing. I also had no intention of letting a nigga
touch my island because he liked the sound of paperwork.

4
00:01:10,579 --> 00:01:25,297
Rusk approached carrying a silver tray and the expression of a man
hoping I had learned one custom in his country. "Your pledge,
Captain." I put Vesper's Ferrari key on the tray. The nigga didn't
even look down.

5
00:01:25,547 --> 00:01:51,311
"The destroyed vehicle does not qualify." "Nigga, you recognized it by
sound?" "I recognized your face preparing to make my morning
difficult." Shawna slid the harbor photograph beside the key. The
Ferrari hung in the air above the dock. A nigga looked magnificent
inside a very expensive problem. Rusk looked down now. "That is a
picture of the destruction." "Before," Shawna said.

6
00:01:51,561 --> 00:02:17,131
"Important distinction." Tank leaned over his shoulder. "Look at the
nigga's posture." "There is no financial value in posture." A man in
velvet stopped beside us. "Is that the actual car?" Rusk closed his
eyes. My wife smiled. "Available pieces of it," I said. "Two million."
"It is a pledge," Rusk said. "There is a procedure." "Three," said
somebody behind the velvet coat.

7
00:02:17,381 --> 00:02:40,619
Nigga, Rusk's tray had become a marketplace without his consent. The
velvet man lifted the photograph and tilted it toward the light.
Behind him sat a green Ferrari looking so clean I felt personally
invited to complicate it. "Four million," he said. I touched the roof
of the green car. "And this." His companion laughed into her drink.

8
00:02:40,869 --> 00:03:02,050
He looked at her, then back at me. A dangerous little pause. The nigga
had money, an audience, and a woman enjoying his hesitation. "Running
condition?" I added. "Naturally." "Nigga, nothing natural about this
room. Keys." He laid them in my hand. We shook. Four million and a
running Ferrari for the wreck.

9
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:21,646
Shawna took the photograph back long enough to write the date across
its border, then gave it to him with both our signatures. "There.
Provenance." "Thank you," he said. Rusk stared at his empty tray.
"Your pledge remains unresolved." "Nigga, let me enjoy being solvent
in motion.

10
00:03:21,896 --> 00:03:43,985
We'll get there." Tank took the new keys from me, checked the car, and
came back shaking his head. "Nigga, it even smells new." Mercedes
looked at Porsche. "We should crash something famous." "You already
dated a musician." "That nigga was famous locally." "So was the
damage." The velvet man's companion nearly dropped her glass laughing.

11
00:03:44,235 --> 00:03:59,582
He tried to recover her attention by explaining the rarity of the
wreck he'd bought. She patted his sleeve. "Darling, everybody saw you
buy it. You can stop selling it to yourself." Nigga, I liked her
before I knew her name.

12
00:03:59,832 --> 00:04:24,979
The man in velvet was Lord Corvin Ash, a collector of cars, swords,
paintings, and women who eventually escaped with at least one of the
first three. His current companion, a twenty-nine-year-old sculptor
named Dalia, shook Shawna's hand and asked whether the opera house had
room for a marble bust of a woman looking disappointed. "Of him?"
Shawna asked. Dalia smiled.

13
00:04:25,229 --> 00:04:50,136
"Beside him." Corvin pretended not to hear. The auction began with a
yacht, continued through three islands none of which were mine, and
reached a red sports car with a silver roof. Its owner, Prince
Laurent, stood beside it looking miserable. Mercedes went still.
"That's the nigga from the hotel." "The bouquets?" I asked. "The
bouquets, the apologies, the terrible choices.

14
00:04:50,386 --> 00:05:15,940
Yes." Laurent saw us and looked away. That interested me more than the
car. The auctioneer was a fast-talking man named Enzo Quill. He wore a
green suit, white gloves, and an expression that had never met a price
it considered final. "The prince offers his family's last racing car,"
he announced. "A magnificent pledge of confidence." Porsche leaned
toward Laurent as we approached.

15
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:41,367
"Your last car?" "It is a complicated family matter." "Nigga, that's
how men introduce simple lies," Mercedes said. "What happened?" He
glanced at Enzo. "My father lost a wager. Enzo purchased the debt. If
I don't place in the tournament, he takes the house." "And if you do?"
"He takes the prize." I looked at the auctioneer. "That nigga good at
math." Laurent's jaw tightened.

16
00:05:41,617 --> 00:06:03,731
"I am not asking for help." "Nigga, you think I waited for your
permission to notice you miserable?" "A prince has obligations." "So
does a nigga with friends. We both standing here. Which one got the
better offer?" Laurent looked at Mercedes. She folded her arms. "Don't
start borrowing dignity to pay that nigga interest," she told him.

17
00:06:03,981 --> 00:06:27,178
"Tell Aiden the truth." Enzo came over smiling. "Captain. Shall I put
you down for a bid?" "Depends. How much for the prince?" His smile
sharpened. "His obligations are not among today's lots." "Nigga,
everything was for sale five minutes ago. This city changes customs
fast." People gathered around us. Enzo knew an audience was money.

18
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:50,428
He also knew Corvin had just paid me four million for a wreck with my
photograph beside it. He named a number. A stupid number. Tank laughed
in his face. "Nigga, for that we can get a whole other prince and
raise his self-esteem from scratch." Laurent looked offended, then
couldn't keep the smile off his face. I pointed at the old station
clock.

19
00:06:50,678 --> 00:07:13,500
"One race. You and me. Around the harbor road and back through the
north gate. I win, you release the debt. You win, you get the four
million from my Ferrari." Enzo's eyes flicked toward Zero, watching
from the upper platform. Then he nodded. "And your new car." "Nigga,
you haven't even seen me drive the old one." The station changed in
five minutes.

20
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:35,826
Music stopped. Doors opened. Men who had been pretending to appreciate
antiques suddenly remembered they loved engines. Ardent's police
cleared the route because he claimed it would prevent disorder, which
was a beautiful way of describing what he was about to encourage.
Shawna kissed me through the window of the green Ferrari.

21
00:07:36,076 --> 00:08:00,730
"No hood riding." "I'm inside this time." "Stay ambitious about that."
Laurent climbed into the passenger seat before I could ask. "I know
the road." "Nigga, you know how to hold on?" "I intend to learn."
Mercedes leaned into his window. "When this nigga turns, you breathe.
When this nigga flies, you shut your mouth so your prayer stays
inside." Laurent stared at her.

22
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:22,484
"Flies?" "Nigga, you entered the passenger seat of a solution. Stop
interviewing the weather." Enzo drove a black racing coupe with his
name painted on the side. Nigga had branded the evidence of his own
bad judgment. The flag fell. We left the station side by side, engines
tearing the afternoon open.

23
00:08:22,734 --> 00:08:46,382
Enzo took the first turn tight, forcing me wide toward a row of empty
stalls. I clipped a basket of oranges. Fruit bounced behind us.
Laurent ducked one that came through the window and caught another
against his chest. "Keep it," I said. "Nigga needs a race souvenir."
"I need my heart back where it was!" "That nigga can sit with the
orange.

24
00:08:46,632 --> 00:09:11,427
Where we going?" "Left at the fountain!" I went left. Enzo went right.
Laurent stared. "That's the longer road." "Nigga got a shorter
conscience. Watch." A delivery truck rolled into our route. I saw it
early enough to choose between crashing and doing something the
Ferrari's designers had probably discussed while drunk and then
crossed out. I chose the second thing.

25
00:09:11,677 --> 00:09:35,310
We hit a low loading ramp, jumped the corner of the truck bed, and
landed on the road beyond with a noise like a rich man's savings
account cracking in half. Laurent made a prayer out of several
languages. "Nigga, pick one god and give him directions!" Enzo
reappeared ahead of us at the next intersection. Smiling. He thought
the truck had solved his problem.

26
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:59,716
I pulled alongside. His smile left first. Then his mirror. The cars
touched. Metal scraped. We raced beneath the old city gate with inches
between our doors and the stone. Above us, people leaned from windows
shouting my name. One woman threw a scarf. It wrapped around Enzo's
aerial like his car had decided to surrender fashionably.

27
00:09:59,966 --> 00:10:25,294
The final stretch ran through the station's covered loading yard. Enzo
cut in front of me and braked. Laurent shouted. I turned into the
empty lane beside him, rode the Ferrari along the raised platform
edge, and came down ahead just before the finish line. The station
erupted. I stopped under the Crown's glass case. Enzo kept going into
a stack of velvet display chairs.

28
00:10:25,544 --> 00:10:50,075
Nigga, he had finally bought himself a seat. Laurent climbed out
shaking. Mercedes and Porsche reached him first. One checked his face.
The other took the orange from his hand and peeled it while he tried
to explain what had happened to his understanding of speed. Enzo
staggered from his car. "The race was irregular!" I leaned against the
Ferrari. "Nigga, your truck missed.

29
00:10:50,325 --> 00:11:14,169
That's irregular for you." "You left the road!" "Your nigga put a
truck on it. I went where the nigga wasn't. That's racing with good
judgment." Laurent lifted his orange. "He caught this too," he
announced, then looked down. "No. I caught it. He made me keep it."
"See?" I said. "Nigga already remembering his own achievements. Sign
his paper." The crowd laughed.

30
00:11:14,419 --> 00:11:35,998
Zero did not intervene. That was how I knew the auctioneer wasn't
worth enough to save. Enzo signed the release on the hood of his own
wreck. Laurent took it with both hands. For a moment the prince looked
younger than twenty-seven, stripped of all the little performances
he'd been using to keep nobody from noticing he was frightened.

31
00:11:36,248 --> 00:11:57,143
"I don't know how to repay you," he said. "Start by choosing a bouquet
for one woman at a time." "That is all?" "Nigga, you tried it yet?
Let's not call the assignment easy before you pass." Mercedes took the
release from him long enough to check the signature, then put it back
against his chest. "That's yours, baby.

32
00:11:57,393 --> 00:12:20,165
This nigga gave you back a future. Quit holding it like somebody
else's receipt." Mercedes and Porsche laughed. Enzo tried to leave in
a second car. I stopped him. "Where you going with that?" "It is
mine." "You owe me a running car." "That was not part of our wager."
"Nigga, I bought it while you was crashing. Ask the auctioneer." His
mouth opened.

33
00:12:20,415 --> 00:12:44,288
Behind him, the entire station began chanting my name. He handed over
the keys. Sometimes a man signs because of a contract. Sometimes he
signs because a thousand people have just realized what kind of nigga
he is, and the door has become more valuable than the car. Corvin
stopped me before I reached the new car. Captain. A small favor.

34
00:12:44,538 --> 00:13:08,400
Nigga, I just sold you a wreck. You want it damaged in a particular
direction? He held out a silver pen. A signature. On the photograph.
For the collection. Dalia stood beside him with her arms folded,
enjoying every second of a man who usually bought other people's
attention trying to ask for mine without showing how badly he wanted
it. I took the pen.

35
00:13:08,650 --> 00:13:33,062
Where? Anywhere you like. Nigga, that's how the Ferrari ended up there
in the first place. Porsche laughed. Mercedes took the photograph from
him and held it flat while I signed. Then she looked at the picture
properly. Aiden, baby. Your face. What about it? You look offended by
the landing. Landing came up fast. Nigga prefers an introduction.
Corvin leaned closer, delighted.

36
00:13:33,311 --> 00:13:56,837
May I quote that beside the display? I looked at him. Dalia started
laughing before I answered. Nigga, put the whole conversation up if
the wall's big enough. He took the photograph back with both hands. I
had seen men carry diamonds with less care. Beside him, Laurent looked
from the picture to the debt release in his own hands and began
smiling again. What?

37
00:13:57,087 --> 00:14:20,643
Mercedes asked him. The prince shook his head. Nothing. I came here
terrified of losing my family's car. And? He looked at me. This man
sold one that no longer worked and bought me back with another. Nigga,
Porsche said, you finally watching the right part of the evening.
Laurent nodded. Folded the release carefully. Put it inside his jacket
over his heart.

38
00:14:20,893 --> 00:14:43,815
I watched him do it and let myself enjoy something I couldn't have
parked in any garage. That night, House Laurent pledged itself to my
claim. The prince arrived at the opera house with one bouquet. He gave
it to Shawna for the lobby and asked Mercedes and Porsche if they
would teach him how to apologize without making it sound like another
invitation.

39
00:14:44,065 --> 00:14:59,261
Porsche looked at Mercedes. "This nigga might be trainable." "Don't
say that in front of him. He'll start fetching." I sat beside my wife
watching the harbor lights move across the water. "How many houses
now?" she asked.

40
00:14:59,511 --> 00:15:17,390
"Enough to make that nigga Zero rearrange his face." "That many?"
"Baby, the nigga needs a whole new expression and a contractor to
install it." She took my hand. "And how many cars?" "Baby, don't ask a
nigga to count when he's trying to be romantic."
